(2073334, 284583, 17507, '<td valign="top">a photo like this invites guesses about the technique-<br/>my guess is that you must have a huge printout of an aerial shot of a suburban area-<br/>if it''s not that, then I have no idea how you did this.<br/> <br/>I''ve ruled out projection, glass-bottomed airplanes, and huge LCD screens<br/> <br/>I haven''t been impressed with a technical tour-de-force so much since labuda''s "Bodhisattva" -<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=154154" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/316/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_154154.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/316/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_154154.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/316/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_154154.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Amazing work! It would be remiss of me to continue without adding this to my favorites! I look forward to seeing this on the front page.</td>', 'a photo like this invites guesses about the technique-my guess is that you must have a huge printout of an aerial shot of a suburban area-if it''s not that, then I have no idea how you did this. I''ve ruled out projection, glass-bottomed airplanes, and huge LCD screens I haven''t been impressed with a technical tour-de-force so much since labuda''s "Bodhisattva" -   Amazing work! It would be remiss of me to continue without adding this to my favorites! I look forward to seeing this on the front page.', '2006-01-23 03:25:43.000000', NULL, 1),
