(2098976, 284770, 43774, '<td valign="top">I love the girl and the colours, I don''t like the slight tilt of the photo, I find it really distracting.</td>', 'I love the girl and the colours, I don''t like the slight tilt of the photo, I find it really distracting.', '2006-01-29 17:05:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2098977, 282241, 43774, '<td valign="top">Interesting, good work.</td>', 'Interesting, good work.', '2006-01-29 17:06:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2098980, 284858, 43774, '<td valign="top">Not that this will affect how I score your photo, but I have to point out the red lobster. Live lobsters aren''t red, they get red after they are cooked. So your creek would be stocked with cooked lobsters which go bad really really quickly, so not much of a fantasy. Good luck with your entry!</td>', 'Not that this will affect how I score your photo, but I have to point out the red lobster. Live lobsters aren''t red, they get red after they are cooked. So your creek would be stocked with cooked lobsters which go bad really really quickly, so not much of a fantasy. Good luck with your entry!', '2006-01-29 17:07:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2099007, 284821, 47117, '<td valign="top">This is a very cool illusion and my top pick. While I can comment further before challenge end, I do want to say a few more things. One is that the shadow on the bottom right does take away from the image just a bit, as does the apparent eye brow hairs. There is also a bit of noise. However, that is really nitpicking the image.  Also, I''d like to say that even though this is a cool illusion, I prefer it be PP that is only used in challenges such as this, where masking and the like lend themselves together pretty much. I prefer to enter a photo less photoshopped, and not so extreme, keeping with traditional photography as best as possible. This is just my opinion, however, for fantasy, I can see this as appropriate.  It showed lovely imagination brought to life, not unlike the photos we see today where babies are laying in the petal of flowers, which is a darling depiction.  I wouldn''t call this darling, but very "eye catching".  I would be surprised if it didn''t ribbon.  Good luck!!</td>', 'This is a very cool illusion and my top pick. While I can comment further before challenge end, I do want to say a few more things. One is that the shadow on the bottom right does take away from the image just a bit, as does the apparent eye brow hairs. There is also a bit of noise. However, that is really nitpicking the image.  Also, I''d like to say that even though this is a cool illusion, I prefer it be PP that is only used in challenges such as this, where masking and the like lend themselves together pretty much. I prefer to enter a photo less photoshopped, and not so extreme, keeping with traditional photography as best as possible. This is just my opinion, however, for fantasy, I can see this as appropriate.  It showed lovely imagination brought to life, not unlike the photos we see today where babies are laying in the petal of flowers, which is a darling depiction.  I wouldn''t call this darling, but very "eye catching".  I would be surprised if it didn''t ribbon.  Good luck!!', '2006-01-29 17:31:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2099019, 284583, 47117, '<td valign="top">This is a very nice illusion, however, the rug looks a bit too flat, and the hands look unnaturally clenched.  But cool how you got the scenery below! EDITED TO ADD: While going through the challenge entries one more time, and looking more closely at my ribbon choices (in which this is one), I wanted to also add that although this is a nice illusion, I now know what I feel is missing that would have really completed this shot. Had you had a fan to blow her hair back and the dress skirt a bit, and maybe propped up a couple of those long rounded pillows (although a bit harder in texture) under the rug, it would have given more of the illusion the rug was in flight as well as herself.  Also that one tassle in front right that looks like it is hanging down, to me seems out of sorts. I think it really should have been blowing up or back as if the rug was really moving forward.  I''m no master at illusions..LOL..but just thought you may like to know the little details I noticed that were out of sorts.  Good luck! And if you don''t ribbon, I would really be quite amazed. :)</td>', 'This is a very nice illusion, however, the rug looks a bit too flat, and the hands look unnaturally clenched.  But cool how you got the scenery below! EDITED TO ADD: While going through the challenge entries one more time, and looking more closely at my ribbon choices (in which this is one), I wanted to also add that although this is a nice illusion, I now know what I feel is missing that would have really completed this shot. Had you had a fan to blow her hair back and the dress skirt a bit, and maybe propped up a couple of those long rounded pillows (although a bit harder in texture) under the rug, it would have given more of the illusion the rug was in flight as well as herself.  Also that one tassle in front right that looks like it is hanging down, to me seems out of sorts. I think it really should have been blowing up or back as if the rug was really moving forward.  I''m no master at illusions..LOL..but just thought you may like to know the little details I noticed that were out of sorts.  Good luck! And if you don''t ribbon, I would really be quite amazed. :)', '2006-01-29 17:38:14.000000', NULL, 1),
