(2120106, 282937, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Well, on the plus side, viewers felt you met the Challenge and gave you reasonable marks.  <br/> <br/>I''m trying to like the off-center composition and trying to understand the ty-in to the Challenge.  But, for me anyhow, it''s tough.  So perhaps that is where some of your more average votes went.  Esoteric, yes. Quick to catch the meaning, difficult.<br/> <br/>Unfortunately, when our viewers are going through entries and voting, quick to catch the meaning seems to be the way to go.  <br/> <br/>So, while I think the white streak is a touch "hot" perhaps it has a meaning I don''t understand.  <br/> <br/>With that thought, I''ll say that your portfolio is an interesting one and you have lots of images that score almost off the charts.  I''ll look forward to seeing more of your entries in future Challenges.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Well, on the plus side, viewers felt you met the Challenge and gave you reasonable marks.   I''m trying to like the off-center composition and trying to understand the ty-in to the Challenge.  But, for me anyhow, it''s tough.  So perhaps that is where some of your more average votes went.  Esoteric, yes. Quick to catch the meaning, difficult. Unfortunately, when our viewers are going through entries and voting, quick to catch the meaning seems to be the way to go.   So, while I think the white streak is a touch "hot" perhaps it has a meaning I don''t understand.   With that thought, I''ll say that your portfolio is an interesting one and you have lots of images that score almost off the charts.  I''ll look forward to seeing more of your entries in future Challenges.', '2006-02-03 21:37:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2120574, 284583, 29282, '<td valign="top">Thanks very much for all of the detail on how you setup and post processed this shot.  And congrats on the ribbon!</td>', 'Thanks very much for all of the detail on how you setup and post processed this shot.  And congrats on the ribbon!', '2006-02-04 01:10:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2120748, 284563, 29269, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>This is a good example of a photo that provokes the observer to establish a link to the challenge. One thing that is easily overlooked when making such images is the ability of the photographer to put him/herself outside the box of their own thoughts and look at the produced photo with the eyes of someone that does not know about the intent. For example, you know that the book is about the snowwhite, i.e. a fairy tale. For the careful observers that know Icelandic (and you''ve left very little text in focus) it may be obvious that the fairy tale is the link to fantasy. For me, it could have been a political science or a economy book, where little is left to fantasize about. Once the viewer recognizes the topic, then they can start appreciating the obvious link between reading and fantasizing.<br/> <br/>Technicals: You''ve chosen a shallow DOF, and that left only a narrow portion of the glasses and the text in focus. For the Fantasy challenge, I would have preferred to convey fantasizing perhaps slightly differently: instead of having a shallow DOF, I would have gone with uniformly, yet tactfully softened image. That way the viewer could get the feeling of wandering off in the fantasy world while e.g. imagining themselves amidst the events they are reading about.<br/>Choice of monochromatic image works well as it is universally accepted that we imagine/dream in monochrome.<br/> <br/>Border: I haven''t noticed it until I really looked hard at the image. This means that the border is tastefully applied and does not take away from the image.<br/> <br/>-Serge<br/> <br/>edit: separated paragraphs for easier reading<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-02-04 03:27:29.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) This is a good example of a photo that provokes the observer to establish a link to the challenge. One thing that is easily overlooked when making such images is the ability of the photographer to put him/herself outside the box of their own thoughts and look at the produced photo with the eyes of someone that does not know about the intent. For example, you know that the book is about the snowwhite, i.e. a fairy tale. For the careful observers that know Icelandic (and you''ve left very little text in focus) it may be obvious that the fairy tale is the link to fantasy. For me, it could have been a political science or a economy book, where little is left to fantasize about. Once the viewer recognizes the topic, then they can start appreciating the obvious link between reading and fantasizing. Technicals: You''ve chosen a shallow DOF, and that left only a narrow portion of the glasses and the text in focus. For the Fantasy challenge, I would have preferred to convey fantasizing perhaps slightly differently: instead of having a shallow DOF, I would have gone with uniformly, yet tactfully softened image. That way the viewer could get the feeling of wandering off in the fantasy world while e.g. imagining themselves amidst the events they are reading about.Choice of monochromatic image works well as it is universally accepted that we imagine/dream in monochrome. Border: I haven''t noticed it until I really looked hard at the image. This means that the border is tastefully applied and does not take away from the image. -Serge edit: separated paragraphs for easier reading', '2006-02-04 03:26:15.000000', '2006-02-04 03:27:29.000000', 0),
(2121211, 284583, 42456, '<td valign="top">Does she need oxygen at that altitude! just a great shot! Congrats on your ribbon!!</td>', 'Does she need oxygen at that altitude! just a great shot! Congrats on your ribbon!!', '2006-02-04 10:44:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2121306, 282473, 21816, '<td valign="top"><b>*Greetings from the Critique Club*</b> <br/> <br/>My first impression of this is the interesting effect you''ve gone for with the almost pencil-like finish. As mentioned in one of the comments you received, it does in a way remind you of a Geiger drawing. The subject you have gone for is unique to say the least.<br/> <br/>I think where this photo suffered the most was in the voters perceptions of the blown highlights. In a way it blends with the pencil effect so therefore in my opinion it doesn''t distract too much from the overall image. <br/> <br/>You''ve kept most of the important detail in the arm and hand which is most important and both the foreground of the cables and the background of the hand sit nicely in focus. <br/> <br/>Overall this is a really good effort and very unique. Well done on your placing and best of luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/>Neil</td>', '*Greetings from the Critique Club*  My first impression of this is the interesting effect you''ve gone for with the almost pencil-like finish. As mentioned in one of the comments you received, it does in a way remind you of a Geiger drawing. The subject you have gone for is unique to say the least. I think where this photo suffered the most was in the voters perceptions of the blown highlights. In a way it blends with the pencil effect so therefore in my opinion it doesn''t distract too much from the overall image.  You''ve kept most of the important detail in the arm and hand which is most important and both the foreground of the cables and the background of the hand sit nicely in focus.  Overall this is a really good effort and very unique. Well done on your placing and best of luck in future challenges. Neil', '2006-02-04 11:54:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2121417, 284866, 20608, '<td valign="top">There is a story behind this and why i submitted it but it would take too long to tell you and its really boring too.. I put it up for a laugh mate because im a crazy guy.</td>', 'There is a story behind this and why i submitted it but it would take too long to tell you and its really boring too.. I put it up for a laugh mate because im a crazy guy.', '2006-02-04 12:54:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2122659, 284669, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I personally love this shot.  I think it might have received more votes in a different category, I am not sure which one but I think voters were looking for fantasy like we would see on TV.  <br/> <br/>The composition in this shot is excellent.  I love to read the comments and find it very interesting how this shot was taken.  I was wondering what kind of filter you could have possibly used but your approach is something I would not have thought of.  I think the placement and pose of the subject is great not too centered.  The warm glow just gives the shot a nice even flow.   Everything in this shot really does look great.  I could even see this on one of those inspiration posters you see. Great job as usual!</td>', '*Critique Club* I personally love this shot.  I think it might have received more votes in a different category, I am not sure which one but I think voters were looking for fantasy like we would see on TV.   The composition in this shot is excellent.  I love to read the comments and find it very interesting how this shot was taken.  I was wondering what kind of filter you could have possibly used but your approach is something I would not have thought of.  I think the placement and pose of the subject is great not too centered.  The warm glow just gives the shot a nice even flow.   Everything in this shot really does look great.  I could even see this on one of those inspiration posters you see. Great job as usual!', '2006-02-04 21:57:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2122713, 284846, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Ok I had to give you a 9, this is an awesome idea and great shot.  I think all photographers have probably had a fantasy like this.  This was one of the most original ideas that I saw during the challenge.  <br/> <br/>The photography itself struck me as though you were trying to give it more of an old fashion look based on the colors.  I think including the background was important otherwise I personally think the image would have lost some of the depth. The composition  is very nice and complete there is no empty space and the shot doesn''t feel crowded.  I also like how the straps looks so prefect, guess they were stored just right. <br/> <br/>I really think you did excellent and work and if you had more time to edit you would have had the shot just they way you wanted.  But hey 18th place still isn''t too bad. Good work!</td>', '*Critique Club* Ok I had to give you a 9, this is an awesome idea and great shot.  I think all photographers have probably had a fantasy like this.  This was one of the most original ideas that I saw during the challenge.   The photography itself struck me as though you were trying to give it more of an old fashion look based on the colors.  I think including the background was important otherwise I personally think the image would have lost some of the depth. The composition  is very nice and complete there is no empty space and the shot doesn''t feel crowded.  I also like how the straps looks so prefect, guess they were stored just right.  I really think you did excellent and work and if you had more time to edit you would have had the shot just they way you wanted.  But hey 18th place still isn''t too bad. Good work!', '2006-02-04 22:35:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2122798, 284122, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"The Dream of Niagara beside my City" is a very unusual piece.  I would agree that the title is critical to the voters, if they missed the title they probably missed the photo itself.  I think you had an excellent idea and a great fantasy for yourself.  The shot itself is very interesting to look at.  I love the color of the sky, I think it is one of the hard times of day to capture and yours looks great.  I also like the poll standing with a light to give some more focus to the shot.  There are a couple little things right on the top of the water line that were distracting for me. Yet the glow of light from somewhere really brings back your focus.  I think you did a good job.</td>', '*Critique Club* "The Dream of Niagara beside my City" is a very unusual piece.  I would agree that the title is critical to the voters, if they missed the title they probably missed the photo itself.  I think you had an excellent idea and a great fantasy for yourself.  The shot itself is very interesting to look at.  I love the color of the sky, I think it is one of the hard times of day to capture and yours looks great.  I also like the poll standing with a light to give some more focus to the shot.  There are a couple little things right on the top of the water line that were distracting for me. Yet the glow of light from somewhere really brings back your focus.  I think you did a good job.', '2006-02-04 23:06:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2122884, 284541, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/> <br/>Ok I have to say wow, as a Critique Club member I keep getting these wonderful photos to critique. Sometimes this makes it harder, because they are so good, and of course The Enchanted Forest is one of these.  I loved this shot during the challenge and personal thought it would have placed higher, but I guess people were looking for out of the blue fantasy shots.  The composition of this shot is just excellent and the red glow is amazing. Very rarely are you able to and let alone capture this amazing sky color. I think your frame is filled perfectly and if you had cropped it anywhere it would take away from the overall feel of the shot.   I would be extremely proud of this piece, you have done some more excellent work.</td>', '*Critique Club*  Ok I have to say wow, as a Critique Club member I keep getting these wonderful photos to critique. Sometimes this makes it harder, because they are so good, and of course The Enchanted Forest is one of these.  I loved this shot during the challenge and personal thought it would have placed higher, but I guess people were looking for out of the blue fantasy shots.  The composition of this shot is just excellent and the red glow is amazing. Very rarely are you able to and let alone capture this amazing sky color. I think your frame is filled perfectly and if you had cropped it anywhere it would take away from the overall feel of the shot.   I would be extremely proud of this piece, you have done some more excellent work.', '2006-02-04 23:31:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2124391, 284822, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi<br/> <br/>I am Kari from the Critique Club.  The following is a critique for "big".<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Clever, Clever, Clever .. how the hell did he do that!<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I think that for the subject matter and the picture you have choosen to take the composition is really good.  It does not meet the rules that well .. but some of the great photographers never met any rules!  <br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>You have a great imagination and captured the topic extremely well.  I remember the feeling well from childhood.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour, focus, and light):</b> <br/>You are right the flash is a little harsh .. but hey how old is the kid .. he did a great job!<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>First one over six ... fantastic ... grew the vote would take your child getting older and doing the flash a little better .. so overall awesome job.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Fantastic ... I saw this as great during the challenge and am pleased it got you your first over 6 ... keep shooting.<br/> <br/>if you have any questions on the critique feel free to PM me.<br/> <br/>Regards<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi I am Kari from the Critique Club.  The following is a critique for "big". First Impression - the most important one: Clever, Clever, Clever .. how the hell did he do that! Composition: I think that for the subject matter and the picture you have choosen to take the composition is really good.  It does not meet the rules that well .. but some of the great photographers never met any rules!   Subject: You have a great imagination and captured the topic extremely well.  I remember the feeling well from childhood. Technical (Colour, focus, and light): You are right the flash is a little harsh .. but hey how old is the kid .. he did a great job! To grow its vote?: First one over six ... fantastic ... grew the vote would take your child getting older and doing the flash a little better .. so overall awesome job. Summary: Fantastic ... I saw this as great during the challenge and am pleased it got you your first over 6 ... keep shooting. if you have any questions on the critique feel free to PM me. Regards Kari', '2006-02-05 16:13:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2125014, 282220, 28261, '<td valign="top">I will ''reiterate'' what toocool has already stated about the things to LIKE about this image.  High key, Soft Focus, Coloration.<br/> <br/>I have to agree with the crop and rotation/angle of the image, however, seeing the 4th try, I have to say that this image is the better of the two.  Rather than inclusion of more, I fell the image would have been better with less.<br/> <br/>A crop closer to the tearduct and a slight straightening of the image would be just fine.  I would like to see more negative space on the side opposite of the face.  <br/> <br/>Overall, an image that I feel was not properly understood by the voters.</td>', 'I will ''reiterate'' what toocool has already stated about the things to LIKE about this image.  High key, Soft Focus, Coloration. I have to agree with the crop and rotation/angle of the image, however, seeing the 4th try, I have to say that this image is the better of the two.  Rather than inclusion of more, I fell the image would have been better with less. A crop closer to the tearduct and a slight straightening of the image would be just fine.  I would like to see more negative space on the side opposite of the face.   Overall, an image that I feel was not properly understood by the voters.', '2006-02-05 21:42:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2133477, 284698, 50864, '<td valign="top">Thank you to the critique club for your time and dedication.  The lighting was done in a homemade light box.  The frame is made of PVC pipe and a white sheet is over the frame.  Desk lights are shining from the sides through the sheet and one light through the front being careful not to throw a shadow.</td>', 'Thank you to the critique club for your time and dedication.  The lighting was done in a homemade light box.  The frame is made of PVC pipe and a white sheet is over the frame.  Desk lights are shining from the sides through the sheet and one light through the front being careful not to throw a shadow.', '2006-02-08 11:05:07.000000', NULL, 0),
