(2201174, 282241, 41142, '<td valign="top">Visually very striking...<br/> <br/>But: It seriously looks like the whole thing was just photoshopped, by using an image from Terminator 2. (I''ll have to take your word on that I guess). Even if the technique you quote is real, I still have some thoughts over whether it is Okay to print out a photoshopped image, and then to photograph the printout. This is very much  an indirect way of photoshopping, not so?<br/> <br/>Forgive the negative note - you achieved a striking result. Just wondering...</td>', 'Visually very striking... But: It seriously looks like the whole thing was just photoshopped, by using an image from Terminator 2. (I''ll have to take your word on that I guess). Even if the technique you quote is real, I still have some thoughts over whether it is Okay to print out a photoshopped image, and then to photograph the printout. This is very much  an indirect way of photoshopping, not so? Forgive the negative note - you achieved a striking result. Just wondering...', '2006-03-05 08:59:29.000000', NULL, 0),
